          %title Symmetries
          %h2#Symmetries Symmetries
          %p In this chapter we discuss these topics:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#InfinitesimalSymmetriesOfTheLagrangianDensity"} Infinitesimal symmetries of the Lagrangian density
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#InfinitesimalSymmetriesOfThePresymplecticPotentialCurrent"} Infinitesimal symmetries of the presymplectic potential current
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            We have introduced the concept of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theories"} Lagrangian field theories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,\mathbf{L})
            in terms of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L}
            on its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            (def.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalLagrangianDensityOnSecondOrderJetBundleOfTrivialVectorBundleOverMinkowskiSpacetime"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            equipped with some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetries"} symmetries
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences"} equivalences
            of the object that preserve the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            (this is the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erlanger+program"}> Erlanger program
            ”,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Erlangen+program#Klein1872"} Klein 1872
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetries+of+the+Lagrangian+density"} infinitesimal symmetries of the Lagrangian density
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SymmetriesAndConservedCurrents"}
            below) send one
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+history"} field history
            to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal"} infinitesimally
            nearby one which is “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"}> equivalent
            ” for all purposes of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
            which will be of concern
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GaugeSymmetries"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"} variational calculus
            says that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+symmetries+of+the+Lagrangian"} infinitesimal symmetries of the Lagrangian
            correspond to
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+currents"} conserved currents
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noether+theorem"} Noether's theorem I
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NoethersFirstTheorem"}
            below. These conserved currents constitute an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+extension"} extension
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            of symmetries, called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dickey+bracket"} Dickey bracket
          %p
            But in
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DerivativeOfLepageForm"} (?)
            we have seen that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            is just one component, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            0, of an inhomogeneous “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lepage+form"}> Lepage form
            ” which in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            1 is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+potential+current"} presymplectic potential current
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Θ
                    %mi BFV
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta_{BFV}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PresymplecticPotential"} (?)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+BV-complex"} local BV-complex
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DerivedPresymplecticCurrentOfRealScalarField"}
            below.) This means that in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            1 we are to consider infinitesimal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/on-shell"} on-shell
            symmetries of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lepage+form"} Lepage form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi L
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi Θ
                      %mi BFV
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{L} + \Theta_{BFV}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+fields"} Hamiltonian vector fields
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HamiltonianForms"}
            below) and the analog of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noether%27s+theorem"} Noether's theorem I
            now says that these correspond to
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+differential+forms"} Hamiltonian differential forms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            of these infinitesimal symmetries is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket+Lie+n-algebra"} local Poisson bracket
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalPoissonBracket"}
            below).
          %p
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noether+theorem"} Noether theorem
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+Noether+theorem"} Hamiltonian Noether theorem
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+differential+forms"} variational form
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan%27s+homotopy+formula"} homotopy formula
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                %th
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                  physical quantity
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,\,\,
                %th
